# Runtime binaries and caches - not source, do not track.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash. Unanchored, `models/` matches a directory of
# that name at ANY depth, and it silently swallowed the console's entire
# `frontend/src/features/models/` feature module - seven source files - out of
# the commit that first brought the frontend under version control. `git add`
# skips ignored paths without a word, so nothing surfaced until CI failed to
# resolve the imports. These rules describe specific directories at the
# repository root; say so.
/amd/
/models/
unsloth_compiled_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.gocache/

# Generated/runtime state
logs/
state/

# Frontend console dependency tree - installed by `npm ci`, not source.
frontend/node_modules/

# Frontend quality-gate output. Regenerated by `npm run quality:collect` on
# every run and uploaded as a CI artifact; only quality/baseline.json is
# source, because it is the recorded state a change is measured against.
frontend/coverage/
frontend/reports/

# Go build output with no extension. `*.exe` below covers a Windows build, but
# `go build ./cmd/cia-console` on any other GOOS writes a bare `cia-console` -
# an 8 MB binary that neither that rule nor CI's tracked-artifact gate (which
# also matches by extension) would stop `git add -A` from committing.
/cia-console
/cia-edge
/cia-tray
/cia-mcp
/cia-credential

# v2 build output, generated runtime configuration, and local secrets
bin/
dist/
generated/
*.local.yaml
*.local.json
*.local.toml
*.exe
*.zip
*.sha256

# Benchmark workdir build outputs and process logs
benchmarks/**/.gocache/
benchmarks/**/obj/
benchmarks/**/*.dll
benchmarks/**/*.pdb
benchmarks/**/*.log
benchmarks/**/*.err

# Quality-suite scratch. A coding cell writes the model's answer into a compiler
# or test-runner workspace and grades it there; the workspace is scaffolding, not
# evidence. What a report cites lives outside it - qualify-*.json for the grades
# and capture-*/ for the raw request and wire response, which contains the
# generated source verbatim.
#
# Tracking these would also break CI: `gofmt -l .` runs over the working tree,
# and model-written Go is frequently unformatted or, on a truncated generation,
# not parseable Go at all.
benchmarks/**/work-*/
benchmarks/**/node_modules/

# Tokenizer echoes from a retention probe captured with -CaptureDiagnostics.
# The retention suite prefills one corpus of up to ~240k tokens and the /tokenize
# capture holds every token id of it, so a single file runs 2-6 MB and one
# 262144 profile alone produced 55 MB - six times the rest of a whole campaign's
# evidence put together.
#
# Excluded because it is not evidence: the corpus is generated deterministically
# by scripts/v2/eval/fixture_corpus.py, and every retention JSON already records
# the corpus SHA-256 that reproduces it. The graded exchanges - capture-*/
# *-v1_chat_completions.json - stay tracked, and those are what a report cites.
benchmarks/**/*-tokenize.json
